From: Amphora <amphora@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] u_gralloc/fallback: detect Qualcomm UBWC without the gmsm magic

Newer Qualcomm gralloc no longer writes the 'gmsm' magic in front of the
private handle ints, so the fallback backend never reads the UBWC flag and
leaves the modifier at DRM_FORMAT_MOD_INVALID.

Amphora's AHB import swapchain (usage 0xB00, tiling=OPTIMAL) resolves the
buffer layout through this fallback: android-stub builds have no IMapper
backend and the qcom backend needs a legacy gralloc HAL. With
DRM_FORMAT_MOD_INVALID + OPTIMAL, tu_image_init picks a tiled/UBWC layout
for a linear buffer. Read the UBWC bit whenever the handle carries the two
ints, so the modifier becomes QCOM_COMPRESSED or LINEAR.

Source: WinNative-Emu/Drivers patches/fix_gralloc_flushall.py (WN-Turnip
1.06-b, our previous passing baseline). Still not upstream in 26.3.0-rc3 or
main.
---
--- a/src/util/u_gralloc/u_gralloc_fallback.c
+++ b/src/util/u_gralloc/u_gralloc_fallback.c
@@ -148,9 +148,12 @@
    out->strides[0] = stride;
 
 #ifdef HAS_FREEDRENO
-   uint32_t gmsm = ('g' << 24) | ('m' << 16) | ('s' << 8) | 'm';
-   if (hnd->handle->numInts >= 2 && hnd->handle->data[hnd->handle->numFds] == gmsm) {
-      /* This UBWC flag was introduced in a5xx. */
+   /* UBWC flag detection - bypass legacy gmsm magic check for A8XX/A840.
+    * Newer Qualcomm gralloc no longer writes the 'gmsm' header.
+    * Without this fix, UBWC buffers are treated as linear -> horizontal lines.
+    */
+   /* This UBWC flag was introduced in a5xx. */
+   if (hnd->handle->numInts >= 2) {
       bool ubwc = hnd->handle->data[hnd->handle->numFds + 1] & 0x08000000;
       out->modifier = ubwc ? DRM_FORMAT_MOD_QCOM_COMPRESSED : DRM_FORMAT_MOD_LINEAR;
    }
